  "body": "Stacked on #2779 (merge #2779 first)\n\nProcess change: yes\n\n## What changed\n\n- `cargo xtask gate batch` builds each crate alone first. There is one `debug build: <crate> (--no-run)` step for each crate.\n- The batch tier then runs its suite steps in the parallel lanes that the release tier uses (`xtask/src/queue.rs`).\n- A quick gate that falls back to the batch plan uses the lanes too.\n- The batch queue takes its order from the newest `timings.tsv` of a `batch-*` or `release-*` run. The release queue reads `release-*` runs only, as before.\n- The `heavy` tier of #2779 and a quick plan stay one step at a time.\n- `AGENTS.md` (batch row of the tier table) and the `gate` skill describe the new batch tier.\n\nThe gate keeps its guarantees. Each step runs and has its own log. A red step fails the gate. A failed build stops the run. The checkout is read before each step (VOID). The builds, the `ISOLATED` targets, each ui step and clippy run alone with the whole job budget.\n\n## Cause\n\n- `Run::plan` used the lane queue only when the label was `release`. The batch tier ran each step after the other.\n- `plan::batch` had one `--no-run` build for all the crates. `crates/kernel` has a dev-dependency on itself with the `truck` feature. The one build gave the shared dependencies the features of all the crates. A later step with one `-p <crate>` resolved a smaller feature set, and cargo compiled that crate again.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins (all in `xtask`, red before the fix):\n\n- `step_tests::batch_prebuilds_each_crate_without_mixing_feature_sets`\n- `step_tests::batch_prebuild_leaves_suite_steps_fresh_with_truck_dev_dep`\n- `lanes_tests::batch_executor_overlaps_lanes_runs_isolated_alone_and_writes_timings`\n- `lanes_tests::batch_history_reads_newest_batch_or_falls_back_to_release`\n- `tests::batch_skips_slow_binaries_and_release_runs_everything` (updated: it pins the first batch step)\n\nMutation results:\n\n| Mutation | Pin | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `xtask/src/plan.rs` from #2779 (one build for all the crates) | the two `batch_prebuild*` tests and `batch_skips_slow_binaries_and_release_runs_everything` | red; green after the restore |\n| `Run::new`: `lanes` on for `release` only | `batch_executor_overlaps_lanes_runs_isolated_alone_and_writes_timings` | red; green after the restore |\n| `lanes::history_for`: `batch` reads `release-*` only | `batch_history_reads_newest_batch_or_falls_back_to_release` | red; green after the restore |\n\nGate on head `1da2bcca2`:\n\n- `cargo test -p xtask`: 213 tests pass (191 unit, 22 integration).\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (1 step, `xtask unit tests`).\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings`: no warnings.\n- `cargo xtask gate batch --dry-run`: 929 steps. 9 builds run alone, 871 steps are in the queue, 49 steps run alone.\n\n## Wall time\n\nOne real `cargo xtask gate batch` run on head `1da2bcca2`: green, 929 steps, 0 failed.\n\n| Reading | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Machine | 8 cores, shared with other agent builds. The load average was 16 to 31 during the run. |\n| Job budget | 6 (the default): 3 lanes x `-j 2` |\n| Wall time | 104.5 min |\n| Sum of the step times (`summed lane wall time`) | 14993 s = 249.9 min |\n| Ratio | 2.4 |\n| Builds and clippy (alone) | 716 s. 8 of the 9 crate builds were warm from a stopped run. |\n| Longest step | `motion suites: lib`, 2472 s. The issue gives 287 s for it on the post-merge runner. |\n\n- This is not a clean benchmark. The other builds on the machine made each step about 8 times slower than on the runner.\n- There is no \"before\" run on this machine. The sum of the step times is an estimate of a run with one step at a time. It is not a measurement.\n- The step logs show that the crate builds do their work. Only `09-debug_build_ui` and `929-clippy` have a `Compiling` line. No suite step compiled a crate.\n- The previous worker measured 45.2 min for the same code with a cold `target/` and a job budget of 6 (comment on #2727). The sum of the step times was 5640 s = 94 min there.\n- A run on the 16-core machine of the issue, before and after, is not done.\n\nThe compile cache was off for this run (`env -u RUSTC_WRAPPER CAMCRAFT_NO_SCCACHE=1`). The sccache server of the machine did not answer. `CAMCRAFT_NO_SCCACHE=1` alone does not help when the environment already sets `RUSTC_WRAPPER`: `exec::cache_env` only declines to add the wrapper.\n\n\nMeasured on the post-merge runner hardware (wopr: Ryzen 9 5950X, 16 cores / 32 threads, 125 GB; warm local sccache), same head `1da2bcca2`, all green, 929 steps:\n\n| Run | Wall time |\n|---|---|\n| Current serial batch tier (post-merge gate on main e5b0ca3c1) | 73 min |\n| This PR, default budget 6 | **30.8 min** |\n| This PR, `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=32` | **14.4 min** |\n\nThe 8-core run above shared its machine with other agent builds (load 16-31), so its wall time is not representative.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No `.nc` or `.cl` file changes.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A 16-core machine. The measurement machine has 8 cores.\n- Windows and macOS.\n- The post-merge runner (`post-merge.yml`).\n- The release tier. Its one debug build for all the crates has the same feature mismatch. This PR does not change the cut gate.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #2779 (`merge-ready`): the `USAGE` text in `xtask/src/main.rs`. The two PRs change adjacent lines, so this branch has a merge of the head of #2779 (`2b40a8435`). #2779 also changes `plan::heavy_steps` in `xtask/src/plan.rs`. That is a different function.\n\nChangelog: The batch gate builds each crate alone and runs its test steps in parallel lanes (#2727).\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2727\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
